Just a minor point, Scott, but this really isn't a good way to get an 
admin to actually look into why you're having a problem and maybe do 
something about it.  ;-)

(Especially since, as far as I can remember, in the previous 8 years f 
this Tournament no one has ever encountered this so I'm not naturally 
disposed to see this as a big deal.)

The Tournament scripts don't attempt to trap any signals, so your SIGINT 
is being passed up through the calling chain to the Perl interpreter 
which sees it as an instruction to kill off the top level process.  This 
can only happen because NetHack itself is choosing not to handle the 
signal and is passing it along, which we didn't anticipate.

This is, however, correct program behavior: all the levels which don't 
have anything that they want to _do_ with a SIGINT are ignoring it and 
allowing it to go up the calling chain.  The only questions, really, are 
why NetHack isn't processing it and do we really want to trap and block it.

I'll look into ways to trap signals in a Perl script, though; please let 
us know which server you're playing on and I'll make sure we put a fix 
on that one first so you can confirm it before we roll it to the others.

Thanks,
